---
layout: default
---
{%- comment -%}
  About, written in Markdown (_pages/about.md): what comes before the first ## heading is the bio, beside the portrait;
  the rest (contact, links, education...) follows below it. A definition list shows as details, a paragraph followed by
  {: .links} as a row of links.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign parts = content | replace: '<dl>', '<dl class="facts">' | split: '<h2' -%}
<section class="view" data-page="about">
  <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
  <div class="about">
    <div class="plate">{% if page.portrait %}<img src="{{ page.portrait | relative_url }}" alt="{{ site.first_name }} {{ site.last_name }}">{% else %}<span>Portrait</span>{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="bio">{{ parts | first }}</div>
  </div>
  {% for part in parts offset: 1 %}<h2{{ part }}{% endfor %}
</section>
